## sn38.1
sn38.1:1.1 | S: At one time Venerable Sāriputta was staying in the land of the Magadhans near the little village of Nālaka. | T: On one occasion Ven. Sāriputta was staying in Magadha near Nāla Village.
sn38.1:1.2 | S: Then the wanderer Jambukhādaka went up to Venerable Sāriputta and exchanged greetings with him. | T: Then Jambukhādaka the wanderer went to Ven. Sāriputta and, on arrival, exchanged courteous greetings with him.
sn38.1:1.3 | S: When the greetings and polite conversation were over, he sat down to one side and said to Sāriputta: | T: After an exchange of friendly greetings & courtesies, he sat to one side. As he was sitting there he said to Ven. Sāriputta:
sn38.1:2.1 | S: “Reverend Sāriputta, they speak of this thing called ‘extinguishment’. | T: “‘Unbinding, unbinding,’ it is said, my friend Sāriputta.
sn38.1:2.2 | S: What is extinguishment?” | T: Which unbinding (are they referring to)?”
sn38.1:2.3 | S: “Reverend, the ending of greed, hate, and delusion | T: “The ending of passion, the ending of aversion, the ending of delusion:
sn38.1:2.4 | S: is called extinguishment.” | T: This is called unbinding.”
sn38.1:2.5 | S: “But, reverend, is there a path and a practice for realizing this extinguishment?” | T: “But is there a path, is there a practice for the realization of this unbinding?”
sn38.1:2.6 | S: “There is, reverend.” | T: “Yes, there is a path, there is a practice for the realization of this unbinding.”
sn38.1:2.7 | S: “Well, what is it?” | T: “Then what is the path, what is the practice for the realization of this unbinding?”
sn38.1:2.8 | S: “It is simply this noble eightfold path, that is: | T: “Precisely this noble eightfold path, my friend:
sn38.1:2.9 | S: right view, right purpose, right speech, right action, right livelihood, right effort, right mindfulness, and right immersion. | T: right view, right resolve, right speech, right action, right livelihood, right effort, right mindfulness, right concentration.
sn38.1:2.10 | S: This is the path, the practice, for realizing this extinguishment.” | T: This is the path, this is the practice for the realization of this unbinding.”
sn38.1:2.11 | S: “Reverend, this is a fine path, a fine practice, for realizing this extinguishment. | T: “It’s an auspicious path, my friend, an auspicious practice for the realization of this unbinding—
sn38.1:2.12 | S: Just this much is enough for diligence.” | T: enough for the sake of heedfulness.”
sn38.1:2.13 | P: Paṭhamaṁ. | T: (none)

